    "q-2191": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2191",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
