    "q-350053": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350053",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /9}3{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /18$ | $\\pi /9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /9}3{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}3{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
