    "q-13467": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13467",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={x}^{3}$, Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-13467-a",
