    "q-13461": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13461",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-13461-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})+C",
